    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulvīnātus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		pulvinus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>cushion-shaped</i>, <i>having a
				swelling</i> or <i>elevation</i>, <i>swelling</i>, <i>elevated</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulvinatus calyx (juglandis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 22, 24, § 86</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fissura (seminis palmae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					13, 4, 7, § 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labrum scrobis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 22, 35, § 168</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capitula columnarum,</span>”
				<i>cushion-shaped capitals</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 1,
					2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 3</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, columnae,</span>”
				<i>columns with cushion-shaped capitals</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4, 1
						<i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
